# Local agent/session control files. These are per-developer working state -- instructions, tool
# permissions, MCP server definitions, scratch memory -- and none of it belongs to the product.
# MCP/permission files in particular can carry endpoints and tokens, so they are fail-closed here
# rather than relied on to be tidied up by hand.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.windsurfrules
.aider*
.mcp.json
.gemini/
GEMINI.md
.roo/
.roomodes
.continue/
.clinerules
.opencode/
.junie/
.specstory/
.taskmaster/
.trae/
CONVENTIONS.md
repomix-output.xml
copilot-instructions.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md
# Copilot's SUBDIRECTORY forms. The single flat file above misses these entirely.
.github/instructions/
.github/prompts/
.github/chatmodes/
SESSION_*
HANDOFF_*

# Directory-versus-file asymmetry, closed deliberately: each pair below had one half covered above
# and the other missing, which is the shape that lets a leftover through. `.gemini/` was listed
# without GEMINI.md (the analogue of CLAUDE.md); `.windsurfrules` is the LEGACY single-file form and
# current Windsurf writes `.windsurf/rules/*.md` instead.
.windsurf/

# Editor workspace state. `.vs/` was already ignored further up; these three were not.
.vscode/
.idea/
.zed/

# Conflict and patch debris. *.tmp was ignored and these were not, which is backwards: .orig and
# .rej are exactly what a failed `git apply` or merge leaves lying around.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# The Windows `> nul` artefact. A redirect written for cmd and then run under Git Bash creates a
# FILE called nul in the working directory. This repo is Windows-primary and uses both shells, which
# is precisely the condition that produces it.
nul

# Runtime lock directory created by src/Fortunes/label-common.sh. The generated label artefacts
# beside it are already fail-closed; an interrupted run left this one untracked and unignored.
.label-pipeline.lock/

# The app's OWN runtime settings. Named explicitly because the secrets block below did not cover
# them, which left one real way for a key to reach a commit: in PORTABLE mode AppPaths.DataRoot is
# <exe dir>\data, so a portable copy unpacked at the repo root writes data\ai-settings.json straight
# into the tree -- untracked AND unignored, so a `git add -A` would have staged it. Latent today only
# because build output lands in the ignored build/ tree. The key inside is DPAPI ciphertext bound to
# user+machine, so the exposure would be endpoint and model configuration rather than a usable
# credential, but that is not a reason to publish it.
ai-settings.json
chat-history.json
/data/
**/data/ai-settings.json
**/data/chat-history.json

# Secrets. Nothing of the sort is tracked today and the app keeps real keys DPAPI-encrypted under
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\DesktopAICompanion, well outside this tree -- these patterns exist so a stray local
# file cannot become a commit.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
*.jks
*.key
*.snk
*.p8
*.keystore
*.pkcs12
.netrc
_netrc
# Public certificate formats. These normally carry no private material, so they are here for
# symmetry with the private-key list above rather than because they are dangerous: the point of this
# block is that a stray local file cannot become a commit, and asymmetry is how that gets defeated.
*.crt
*.cer
*.der

# The host's own settings file. Sibling of the ai-settings.json block above and ignored for the same
# portable-mode reason: a portable copy unpacked at the repo root writes data\settings.json into the
# tree. AppSettingsStore carries no key, secret or token field, so this is window dressing today --
# which is exactly when to add it, rather than after a field like that appears.
settings.json
**/data/settings.json
.npmrc
.yarnrc
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
secrets.json
secrets/
credentials.json
credential*.json
appsettings.*.local.json
# Suffix form as well as the dotfile: ".env" and ".env.*" above do not match "local.env".
*.env

# Portable app runtime settings store
DesktopPet.config

# Generated fortune-labeling work. These exact paths are also fail-closed in
# the retired release-gate scripts and must never enter a source or release artifact.
/src/Fortunes/label-input.tsv
/src/Fortunes/labels-store.tsv
/src/Fortunes/label-chunks/
/src/Fortunes/.texts
/src/Fortunes/.batchtexts
/src/Fortunes/label-batch.txt

# Local dev/test materials kept under tests/ (screen recordings, audio, sample skins) -- never shipped.
tests/*.mp4
tests/*.mp3
tests/*.zip
tests/*-transcription.md

# Assistant/session working material. These are written OUTSIDE the repo by design, but a stray one
# created in the tree would otherwise be one `git add -A` away from a public release. FORTUNE-SOURCES-
# ASSESSMENT.md used to point at `scratchpad/harvest/...` as though it were committed; it never was.
/scratchpad/
/.scratch/
/scratch/
*.scratch
